---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro'
import { CopyCommand } from '../../components/CopyCommand'
---

<Site title="Getting started" docsSlug={null}>
  <article style="max-width:720px; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:20px;">
    <h1 style="font-size:40px; font-weight:900; letter-spacing:-1px; margin:0;">Getting started</h1>
    <p style="font-size:18px; color:var(--muted); font-weight:700; margin:0;">
      Pouf is distributed as a shadcn-style registry. You install components into your own codebase and own the source — there is no runtime dependency to lock.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size:24px; font-weight:900; margin:16px 0 0;">1. Prerequisites</h2>
    <p style="margin:0; font-weight:700;">A React app with <strong>Tailwind CSS v4</strong> and the <strong>shadcn CLI</strong> configured (a <code>components.json</code>). Pouf's components use Radix primitives, <code>class-variance-authority</code>, and <code>clsx</code> — the CLI installs these for you.</p>

    <h2 style="font-size:24px; font-weight:900; margin:16px 0 0;">2. Install the base</h2>
    <p style="margin:0; font-weight:700;">The base ships the theme file (<code>pouf.css</code>) — tokens, cushion utilities, keyframes, and component chrome. Every component depends on it, so it comes along automatically, but you can add it explicitly:</p>
    <CopyCommand client:load command="npx shadcn@latest add https://pouf.dev/r/base.json" />
    <p style="margin:0; font-weight:700;">Then import it once in your app entry, alongside the font:</p>
    <pre class="code-block">import '@fontsource-variable/nunito'
import './components/pouf/pouf.css'</pre>

    <h2 style="font-size:24px; font-weight:900; margin:16px 0 0;">3. Add a component</h2>
    <CopyCommand client:load command="npx shadcn@latest add https://pouf.dev/r/button.json" />
    <pre class="code-block">{`import { Button } from './components/pouf/Button'

export function Example() {
  return <Button tone="mint">Save</Button>
}`}</pre>

    <h2 style="font-size:24px; font-weight:900; margin:16px 0 0;">The one rule</h2>
    <p style="margin:0; font-weight:700;">
      No component takes a <code>className</code> or <code>style</code> prop. Appearance is chosen with variants (<code>tone</code>, <code>size</code>, <code>variant</code>), so your UI can't quietly drift off-system. When you genuinely need an escape hatch, you own the file — edit it. That is the whole trade Pouf makes: a strong default that holds, with the source in your hands when it shouldn't.
    </p>

    <p style="margin:16px 0 0; font-weight:800;">Next: pick a component from the sidebar to see it live, copy its install command, and read its source.</p>
  </article>
</Site>
